#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048863 :topic/difficulty 0.6044133585735892 :topic/encompasses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186428134 :encompassing/rationale "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account foundations: 1 rises / 1 eligible passed source activities = 1.000000; nearest selected fraction = 1. Crossing activity numbers [1]; waits [1]. Separate account estimates: foundations=1 (1/1). Selection: most observations, then lower weight, then account name; no averaging. Single-activity estimates included. Intervening target updates: False. Crossing frequency is the chosen practical estimate of encompassing coverage; a multi-band rise counts once. This does not interpret color steps as physical repetition units. Method: encompassing-report.md. Evidence: reference/mathacademy/encompassing-analysis-2026-10-11/frequency-fractions/foundations-frequency-estimates.json, pair 1168->29. All account evidence retained in the prepared import's selected-relationships.json." :encompassing/topic {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049304} :encompassing/weight 1.0}] :topic/id #uuid "c769a4f9-fb8c-5389-aac8-802ee9b0afb4" :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100991 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100686 :question/id #uuid "0928c2fa-a772-5d39-a638-1b1d0e71be2f" :question/math-academy-id "e-4378" :question/problem "Calculate $A-(B-C),$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Performing the operations on each corresponding entry, we get:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-(B-C) & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}-(\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-1-0 & -1-(-5) \\\\ 2-1 & 0-1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1-(-1) & 0-4 \\\\ 2-1 & -2-(-1)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -4 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "667ac53c-36b8-56a0-9699-fe27c8373c6b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Sum or Difference of Three or More Matrices"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100992 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100687 :question/id #uuid "1b15db42-aba2-575c-a01e-b715450329fd" :question/math-academy-id "e-4379" :question/problem "Find $A+C-(B+A)$, if\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ \\sqrt{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$B=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$C=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ -6 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>" :question/worked-solution "First, we simplify the expression by distributing the subtraction over the matrices in the parentheses: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+C-(B+A) & =A+C-B-A \\\\  & =\\cancel{A}+C-B-\\cancel{A} \\\\  & =C-B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe are left with a single subtraction. So, we subtract the corresponding entries of the two matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}C-B & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ -6 & 1\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3-3 & -1-(-1) \\\\ 1-2 & 2-0 \\\\ -6-(-4) & 1-1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "16e62b0e-adda-5d35-aeb9-961057dce8f0" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Sum or Difference of Three or More Matrices Using Distributivity"}] :topic/math-academy-id 1168 :topic/title "Properties of Matrix Addition"}]}
